        <title type="html"><![CDATA[setInterval(code) - update with TrustedScript]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41403</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41403"/>
        <updated>2025-10-06T05:38:59.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">This updates the TrustedScript documentation for <code class="notranslate">[Window/setInterval()</code>](<a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Window/setInterval" rel="nofollow">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Window/setInterval</a>) to include information about using it with trusted types.</p>
<p dir="auto">A lot of this was to update the doc to current template - such as moving Usage notes under description and so on.<br>
I also thought it worthwhile to purge mention of getting things to work with IE, and focus on how you get the "this" right rather than not being able to get it right on legacy JavaScript.</p>
<p dir="auto">The security considerations also mention CSP since generally the <code class="notranslate">code</code> option is disabled by default.</p>
<p dir="auto">I will look at <code class="notranslate">setTimeout()</code> after this, since the changes would be mostly the same.</p>
<p dir="auto">Project tracking in <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="2770544982" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/37518" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/37518/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/37518">#37518</a></p>]]></content>
